# What a compiled backend's server runtime hands a request in, and reads a response out of, in plain values only
# (item term-self-host-001-1218). Internal: reached only through the native network/server modules.
#
# A runtime shim (native/<platform>/network/runtime/server.*) is spliced into the emitted program as source, so a Term
# form it names must keep its name there. They did not: a program that also loads network/http (its own `response`)
# has the server's form split by file as `Response__in0_1`, and the rust, swift and kotlin shims that named `Response`
# did not build. So no shim names a Term form: it calls the task the native module hands it with the request's parts,
# and reads back a list of text, `[status, body, name, value, name, value, ...]`, as network/http reads its host's.

load @term/base/network/server/request
  find request

load @term/base/network/server/response
  find response
  find header

# the handler called on a request made of `method` ... `dock`, its response as `[status, body, name, value, ...]`
task answer-plain
  take handler
    like task
      take request, like request
      like response
  take method, like text
  take url, like text
  take path, like text
  take query, like text
  take headers
    like hash
      like text
      like text
  take body, like text
  take dock, like unknown
  like list, like text
  save answered
    call handler
      make request
        bind method, read method
        bind url, read url
        bind path, read path
        bind query, read query
        bind headers, read headers
        bind body, read body
        bind dock, read dock
  save out
    make list
  call out/push
    text <{answered/status}>
  call out/push
    read answered/body
  walk list
    read answered/headers
    hook next
      take site, name one
      call out/push
        read one/name
      call out/push
        read one/value
  send back
    read out
